-- title:
--   Centre pins on special fibres of the Igusa scheme
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $p \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$.
--
--   The function field in play is `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull p)` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series, obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb` of `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$ for the divisors $d \mid p$. Inside it, `jBar p` is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$.
--
--   *Genericity hypotheses on $j$.* The element `jBar p` is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`htrans`), it is nonzero, and `modularFunctionFieldBar p` is finite-dimensional both over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\,$`jBar p`$\,)$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\,$`jBar p`$^{-1})$.
--
--   *Chart comparison hypotheses.* Here `chartAlgFin p ℓ` (respectively `chartAlgInf p ℓ`) is the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of `modularFunctionFieldFull p` of elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ (respectively over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$), and `CurveModel.chartRing K S` denotes the subalgebra of elements integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $S$. Two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra isomorphisms are given,
--   $$e_{\mathrm{fin}} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\ p\ \ell \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathtt{chartRing}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\ \{\mathtt{jBar}\ p\},$$
--   $$e_{\infty} \colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \mathtt{chartAlgInf}\ p\ \ell \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathtt{chartRing}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\ \{(\mathtt{jBar}\ p)^{-1}\},$$
--   together with the normalisations `hFin` and `hInf`: for every $b$ in the respective chart algebra, the image of $1 \otimes b$ under $e_{\mathrm{fin}}$, resp. $e_\infty$, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, is the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of $b$.
--
--   *The generic-fibre identification.* Let $M_\eta$ be `CurveModel.ofGenerator (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (jBar p) htrans`, the curve model of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ glued from the two charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartRing` on $\{j\}$ and on $\{j^{-1}\}$, with its proper smooth structure morphism $M_\eta.\mathtt{toBase}$, its identification of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` with the function field of $M_\eta.C$, and its bijection between closed points and places. The statement then quantifies over every morphism $e_\eta \colon M_\eta.C \to \mathtt{IgusaScheme}\ p\ \ell \times_{\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, assumed to be an isomorphism, such that: $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is $M_\eta.\mathtt{toBase}$ (`heη`); and, on the two charts (`hchartFin`, `hchartInf`), `CurveModel.ι₀` followed by $e_\eta$ and by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the composite of $b \mapsto 1 \otimes b$ with $e_{\mathrm{fin}}$, followed by the Igusa chart immersion `ιFin p ℓ`, and likewise `CurveModel.ιInf` with $e_\infty$ and `ιInf p ℓ`. Here `IgusaScheme p ℓ` is the pushout of the two chart spectra along the overlap and `igusaTo p ℓ` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Under these hypotheses there exist data as follows, indexed by the valuation subrings $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. with $\ell \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$:
--
--   1. ring homomorphisms $\rho_A \colon \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to A$ with $\rho_A$ followed by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$;
--
--   2. curve models $M_{s,A}$ over the residue field $\kappa_A = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A p` (the $\kappa_A$-subfield of $\kappa_A$-Laurent series generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid p$, in characteristic $\ell$);
--
--   3. morphisms $e_{s,A} \colon M_{s,A}.C \to \mathtt{IgusaScheme}\ p\ \ell \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \operatorname{Spec} \kappa_A$, the base change being along $\rho_A$ followed by the residue map, each $e_{s,A}$ an isomorphism, and each satisfying $e_{s,A}$ followed by the second projection $= M_{s,A}.\mathtt{toBase}$;
--
--   such that for every such $A$ with $\kappa_A$ of characteristic $\ell$ and algebraically closed, for every `FibreModel p A ℓ κ_A (residue A)` $\mathit{fm}$ — a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_\infty$ of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull p)` containing the constants from $A$ and the relevant powers of $j$, whose elements are integral over the corresponding affine base rings, equipped with reduction homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}} \colon B_{\mathrm{fin}} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` and $\pi_\infty \colon B_\infty \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` that agree with the residue map on constants and send $j$, $j(q^p)$, $j^{-1}$ to their characteristic-$\ell$ counterparts — for every cusp chart $cc$ for $\mathit{fm}$ (which requires $j(q^p) \cdot j^{-p} \in B_\infty$ and that $\pi_\infty$ send it to the corresponding product in characteristic $\ell$), and under the hypotheses `hfin` and `hinf` that the coefficientwise images of all elements of `chartAlgFin p ℓ` lie in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and those of all elements of `chartAlgInf p ℓ` lie in $B_\infty$, both of the following hold.
--
--   First conjunct (finite chart pin): for every $\kappa_A$-point $y$ of $M_{s,A}$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \kappa_A \to M_{s,A}.C$ whose composite with $M_{s,A}.\mathtt{toBase}$ is the identity, and every ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\ p\ \ell \to \kappa_A$ such that $y$ followed by $e_{s,A}$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec} \beta$ followed by `ιFin p ℓ`, one has for every $b$ in `chartAlgFin p ℓ`: the image of $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $b$, included into `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A p`, lies in the valuation subring of the place $(M_{s,A}).\mathtt{pointEquivPlace}\ y$ attached to $y$ under the bijection between $\kappa_A$-points and places of the function field, and its difference with the image of $\beta(b)$ under $\kappa_A \to$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A p` lies in the nonunits of that valuation subring.
--
--   Second conjunct (pole chart pin): the same assertion with `chartAlgInf p ℓ`, `ιInf p ℓ` and $\pi_\infty$ in place of `chartAlgFin p ℓ`, `ιFin p ℓ` and $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$.
--
--   Thus at each place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $\ell$ the reduction of a chart function through the fibre model agrees, at the place determined by a $\kappa_A$-point, with the value prescribed by the Igusa chart coordinates of that point; the models $M_{s,A}$ and the isomorphisms $e_{s,A}$ are produced before the fibre model is quantified, so the pins hold for every fibre model admitting a cusp chart.
--
--   This is the special-fibre half of the identification of the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with the two-chart model of $X_0(p)$: given a chart-pinned identification of the generic fibre over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, it produces smooth proper models of the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field at each place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $\ell$, together with the centre pins expressing that the Igusa chart coordinates of a $\kappa_A$-point compute the reductions of the chart functions at the corresponding place. It is used in the Deligne–Rapoport level packaging to identify the images of closed points and sections under the two reduction maps with the crossing points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_spBase_and_cuspChart_centrePin_of_genericFibre_iso_ofGenerator.lean

